1
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:04,640
*calm breathing*

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,560
(Forster) Breathe calmly.

3
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,640
In...
*deep inhale*

4
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,960
And out.
*deep exhale*

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:14,840
In.

6
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,960
*deep inhale*

7
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:18,400
And out.

8
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:19,720
*deep exhale*

9
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:21,880
There...

10
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,400
And now...

11
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:27,200
*eerie music*

12
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,760
Fix your eyes on the pendulum.

13
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:38,720
Do not try to order your thoughts.
Simply let them go.

14
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,520
And breathe in calmly...

15
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,640
*deep inhale*

16
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,920
...and out.

17
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:52,080
*explosion, dramatic music*

18
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,800
(Forster) I will guide you.

19
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:56,680
Step by step.

20
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:59,240
Step by step,

21
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:02,000
down to the root of the suffering.

22
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:04,040
Debout!
- To the source of the pain.

23
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:05,200
Debout!

24
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:08,440
*light switch clicks*

25
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:10,800
(Forster) Now focus
all your strength

26
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,280
and direct it
upon the stone in your hand.

27
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:19,400
Your hand obeys your will.

28
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:22,880
Your will
can crush that stone.

29
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,240
*whimpering*

30
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,160
To your will alone

31
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:28,400
does your hand submit.

32
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:32,680
And when you open your hand now,
you will see,

33
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,360
your hand is as calm as mine.

34
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:38,120
Breathe in calmly...

35
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,120
*music intensifies dramatically*

36
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,560
...and out.

37
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:46,720
And when I say 'now',
you will let go.

38
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:47,920
Now.
*he starts up*

39
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:49,600
*music fades out*

40
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,720
*soft rustling*

41
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,040
How can I ever thank you, Doctor?

42
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:05,040
*distant rumbling*

43
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:07,880
How far did you get in your studies,

44
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:09,280
as an assistant doctor?

45
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:15,080
Emergency exam in the second year of war.

46
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,560
Then the Western Front.

47
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:24,720
Why don't you lend me a hand
here at the clinic for a while?

48
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:28,640
Until you have fully recovered
and I have to let you go.

49
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,960
I could use someone like you.

50
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,400
Comrades,

51
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:37,320
it is my duty to inform you,

52
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,560
that today
our Kaiser Wilhelm has abdicated.

53
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:45,680
He and his family have fled the country.

54
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:51,520
In Berlin, the Social Democrat Scheidemann
has proclaimed the Republic.

55
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:56,160
After four years of bloodshed,
the war is over.

56
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:57,600
(Soldier) What will become of us?

57
00:02:57,680 --> 00:02:59,960
Germany has surrendered.

58
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,440
That is not true!

59
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:04,360
(Hitler) That's a lie!

60
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:06,240
Lies, all of it!

61
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,400
(Doctor) Silence.

62
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:09,000
You traitors!

63
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,840
You Jew-ridden scum!
- Come along.

64
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,040
Lies, all of it!

65
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:15,320
You liars!
- Sit down.

66
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,640
(Hitler) You traitors!

67
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:20,640
You Jew-ridden... scum!

68
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,960
(mumbles) Miserable rabble.

69
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:26,440
You will crawl in the dirt,
you filthy worms...

70
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:28,840
(Anno) Can he be helped?

71
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:32,080
He won't last long around here,
the troublemaker.

72
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:34,880
(Forster) His eyes
are completely intact.

73
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:37,240
Yet he truly sees nothing?

74
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:38,880
The man does not wish to see.

75
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:42,040
We call it hysterical blindness.

76
00:03:42,560 --> 00:03:45,360
The cause is not organic in nature.
- A malingerer.

77
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,040
A sick man.

78
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:49,480
Sick, but not blind.

79
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:53,160
Hey! Lance Corporal?

80
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:55,720
Staff Surgeon, Professor, sir.

81
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:57,520
Come over here.

82
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:02,840
Over here.

83
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,320
Why are you still awake?

84
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:14,480
Can't sleep, Professor, sir.
Not for weeks.

85
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,880
Nerves, is it?
A bit frayed?

86
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,480
Please, Staff Surgeon, sir,

87
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:23,560
help me.
I want to be able to sleep again.

88
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:26,200
Go into the anteroom
and wait for me there.

89
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:27,600
Thank you, Professor, sir.

90
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:29,720
When...?
- Let him wait.

91
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:34,960
*man speaking in background*

92
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,240
A good subject,

93
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:46,880
yet full of obstinacy.
We'll let him wait.

94
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:50,640
(Anno) All night?
- Yes. He must want it.

95
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,200
He must yearn for it with every fiber
of his body

96
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:55,320
and his soul.

97
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,920
Let him hope all night
that we will come.

98
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:03,040
He isn't ready yet,
but tomorrow morning we shall release him.

99
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,160
*tense music*

100
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:10,280
(Forster)
In every man lies a god.

101
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:12,320
That is the will.

102
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,800
That is the energy.

103
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:18,040
The flame.

104
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,440
Do you see the flame?

105
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:24,040
I want to, but...

106
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:25,600
Yes.

107
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,360
Yes.
- You must see.

108
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,960
Anything is possible for you.

109
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,240
More!

110
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,400
More.

111
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:37,720
More!
- *Hitler cries out*

112
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,040
*music subsides*

113
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,440
Good, that's good!

114
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,360
Stand up.

115
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,200
What do you see now?

116
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,000
White? Paper? I...

117
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:54,520
I see white...

118
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:56,880
*Hitler pants*

119
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,040
You see.

120
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,680
*eerie music*

121
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:28,720
*rhythmic music*

122
00:06:47,160 --> 00:06:49,680
*excited chatter,
street noise*

123
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,600
*opulent orchestral music*

124
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,480
Thank God, there you are.

125
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:34,800
Only you can testify to my information.

126
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:37,680
Down there at the bar
is Editor-in-Chief Heymann.

127
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,600
We'll speak with him.
- No.

128
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:45,160
You cannot trust him anymore.

129
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,920
There is a warrant out for your arrest.

130
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:58,200
Anno, what is going on here?

131
00:07:58,640 --> 00:07:59,920
There he stands, up there.

132
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:03,000
We must leave right this minute.

133
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,240
*music intensifies dramatically*

134
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:11,840
*dynamic music*

135
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:25,480
*music fades out*

136
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:28,680
(Blank) Come on. Up and around.

137
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:30,640
*tense music*

138
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:32,120
Anno, what is going on?

139
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:35,320
Gereon, his knowledge
has more explosive power than any bomb.

140
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:36,960
Come on.

141
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,080
*engine starts*

142
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,240
Up ahead.

143
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:49,560
In Germany, no one will publish
your story anymore.

144
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:53,480
Certainly not now
that you are wanted by the police.

145
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:56,400
You must go abroad, immediately.

146
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:58,880
The express train to Paris
departs shortly.

147
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,000
You have to catch it.

148
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:04,600
I will get in touch
with Dr. Ernst Weiß.

149
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,320
He is familiar with your story.

150
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:08,320
He has all the necessary
connections to the press.

151
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:09,680
How do you imagine this working?

152
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,000
The police are hunting me.

153
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:15,160
I won't even make it onto the train,
let alone to France.

154
00:09:16,840 --> 00:09:18,120
I will accompany you.

155
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,160
Why should I trust a policeman?

156
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,400
He is my brother.

157
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:31,960
Ask for Dr. Weiß
at this establishment.

158
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:35,840
It's the regular hangout of the Germans
in the 5th Arrondissement.

159
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,080
Tell him everything.
I can verify it at any time.

160
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,760
Put these on.

161
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:44,960
For cover.

162
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:46,880
Well?

163
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,640
Searched everywhere.

164
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,200
He must have arrested him.

165
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,720
The doctor?

166
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,680
Then he probably took him
to the Burg, didn't he?

167
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:56,960
Safe to assume, yes.

168
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,160
*crowd sings boisterously*

169
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,720
A magnificent sight.

170
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:20,240
The outstretched arms, the shouts of 'Heil'.

171
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:23,520
The Stahlhelm veterans
raise their arms in salute too.

172
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,000
Just like the SA.

173
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:28,760
It is a unified whole,
expressed here in its entirety.

174
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:31,200
*men sing marching song*

175
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:39,840
*dynamic music*

176
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,120
*clamor of voices, whistle blows*

177
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:46,000
Make room there.
- Out of the way.

178
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:49,240
The train is packed, stand back.
- We have to get on this train.

179
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:52,000
My husband has been picked up.

180
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:54,560
(Man) Wait!

181
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,440
*chaotic shouts*

182
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:01,280
I'm sorry. The train is completely full,
nothing to be done.

183
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,600
Conductor!

184
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:05,000
We are conducting an official transfer
abroad.

185
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:07,680
My colleague must come along too.
Not alone, unfortunately.

186
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,560
Right away, Detective.

187
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:11,960
Inspector, thank you.

188
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:14,240
If you would follow me, please.
Colleague!

189
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:17,280
*music continues*

190
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:23,520
Good evening,
pardon the intrusion.

191
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,640
The window seats are requisitioned.

192
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:27,000
We booked reservations.

193
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,560
Official duty is force majeure.
- This is outrageous.

194
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,640
I must ask you.

195
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,280
A window seat isn't necessary.

196
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:35,280
Yes it is, Inspector, you shall have it.
I must ask you to stand up.

197
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,400
This is an important prisoner transfer.

198
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:40,840
We will remain on the train, however.
- Naturally, Monsieur.

199
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:42,720
I apologize, Madame. Have a good journey.

200
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:46,720
Good evening.

201
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,080
Good evening.

202
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:49,800
Good evening.

203
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:52,040
*door closes*

204
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,120
May I?

205
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,360
Don't worry.

206
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:05,360
The man is... under control.

207
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:07,800
(Passenger) Mhm.
- (Conductor) Stand back.

208
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:09,880
*locomotive bell clangs, hubbub*

209
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,880
We have to get through!
We must reach that train!

210
00:12:14,200 --> 00:12:16,240
(Policeman) Out of the way,
that is an order!

211
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:26,840
Where is this train heading?

212
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:29,000
Paris, but you're too late.

213
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:33,360
Where does it stop?
Along the way, where does it stop?

214
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:35,800
Only in Cologne,
and after that, not until the border.

215
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:39,800
Come with me.

216
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:42,880
*train whistle blows*

217
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:46,440
*gently driving music*

218
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,640
*door opens and closes*

219
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:18,680
*music swells menacingly*

220
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,360
*music fades slowly*

221
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,520
How do you know my brother?

222
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:34,480
I treated him.

223
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:37,800
At the end of the war.

224
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:42,120
Later, he completed his doctorate under me.
Faced a brilliant career.

225
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:45,040
And then he...

226
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:49,440
Yes,
today one would say 'disappeared'.

227
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:53,600
Until he suddenly resurfaced
nearly a decade later.

228
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:55,200
Out of the blue.

229
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:57,720
Under his new identity
as Dr. Schmidt.

230
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:59,720
What did he want?

231
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:03,080
My support.
Your brother saw much of this coming.

232
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:05,040
I did not;
I refused to see it.

233
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:10,040
What will you tell this gentleman
in Paris?

234
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:12,200
What is this about?

235
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,720
A medical file.

236
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,960
Is it about a politician?

237
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:20,760
I'm sorry.

238
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:24,000
I am taking considerable risks for your sake.
No, not for mine.

239
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:26,480
You are doing it for your brother,
aren't you?

240
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:31,000
There is a secret there too.

241
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:36,800
I abandoned my brother at the front.

242
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:40,560
It was only by a miracle that he survived.

243
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,320
That haunts you?

244
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:48,080
To this day.

245
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:53,560
I am a psychiatrist, so...
I am well acquainted with war trauma.

246
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:56,200
Very familiar.

247
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:00,720
Was Hitler your patient?

248
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,800
Yes, I encountered the current
Reich Chancellor back in Pasewalk,

249
00:15:13,880 --> 00:15:16,320
as his physician.

250
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:19,800
Back then, he was still
a simple lance corporal.

251
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:21,880
And?

252
00:15:22,040 --> 00:15:23,720
*eerie music*

253
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:26,560
The psychiatric examinations have...

254
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:31,160
shall we say, they are of a compromising nature.

255
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:33,480
And above all,
and far worse for him,

256
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:37,440
it starkly contradicts his own mythmaking.

257
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,920
What did you want at the Press Ball?

258
00:15:45,680 --> 00:15:47,400
To meet a journalist.

259
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:50,280
To give him the file?

260
00:15:50,880 --> 00:15:53,320
The file has been gone without a trace
for years,

261
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,480
yet if you will...

262
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,680
I am the file.

263
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,880
*mysterious music*

264
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:07,120
Gereon?

265
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:35,480
*music fades out*

266
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,160
*rails squealing*

267
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:55,800
*dark music*

268
00:16:58,280 --> 00:17:00,280
*distant howl*

269
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:18,000
(Policeman) Routine check,
papers please.

270
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:24,520
Routine check, papers.

271
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,160
Routine check, papers please.

272
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:31,320
Good evening, ladies and gentlemen.
Excuse me, identification please.

273
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,720
(Passenger) We haven't even
reached the border yet.

274
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:35,800
Routine check, papers!

275
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,960
*somber music*

276
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:57,840
Kracauer.

277
00:17:58,760 --> 00:17:59,960
You are Jewish?

278
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,880
What does that have to do with anything?
- Yes or no?

279
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:05,600
Who are you, anyway?
- Please, Eleanor.

280
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,680
(Frau Kracauer) If I have to identify myself,
so should he.

281
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:12,560
Please pardon my wife.
And yes, I am Jewish.

282
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:15,360
My wife took my name.

283
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:17,120
Herbert, you must...
- Be quiet!

284
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:21,080
(Herr Kracauer) We are traveling
to my sister's in Paris.

285
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:23,160
We will return next week.

286
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:29,040
Hm. You Jews have relatives
all over the world, don't you?

287
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:30,640
What is going on here?

288
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,120
And you are?

289
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:38,960
Prussian Police.

290
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:43,080
We're in Thuringia here.
One can tell.

291
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,920
As far as I know, there is no border
between Prussia and Thuringia.

292
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:48,520
Or did I miss something?

293
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:50,440
Wise guy, eh?

294
00:18:51,160 --> 00:18:53,560
Identify yourself,
and I will file a formal complaint against you.

295
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,400
*he exhales sharply*

296
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,320
*music subsides*

297
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:19,560
Thank you.

298
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:23,080
*Herr Kracauer weeps*

299
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:32,200
I have no papers on me.
We'll never get to France like this.

300
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:34,000
*music fades out*

301
00:19:34,720 --> 00:19:36,560
Then we will get off in Cologne.

302
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,800
I can procure papers for you there.

303
00:20:01,040 --> 00:20:03,560
*lively music*

304
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:14,080
*train whistle sounds loudly*

305
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:19,840
*music becomes more dynamic*

306
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:43,640
(Conductor) Stand back!

307
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:45,560
*clamor of voices*

308
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:47,480
*Rath laughs*
Rose Monday.

309
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,000
We've arrived just in time.

310
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,280
Or not.

311
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,920
*music fades out*

312
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:05,360
*excited chatter*

313
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:14,240
Other exit. Come along.

314
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:27,080
Now what?

315
00:21:27,560 --> 00:21:29,440
*suspensefully pulsing music*

316
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:31,520
Out the back. I'll follow.

317
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:39,560
Erwin.
- (Erwin) Our suitcase!

318
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:41,960
Conductor! Conductor!

319
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,880
Our suitcase! A thief!

320
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:45,080
Right, let's go.

321
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:48,240
Officers! This way!

322
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:52,760
Move.
- There they are up ahead. Halt!

323
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:54,600
I said halt!

324
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,640
(Policeman) End of the line, gentlemen!

325
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,560
Put it down. Is that your suitcase?

326
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:07,720
What is inside?

327
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:11,120
I haven't the faintest idea.
Hands where I can see them, gentlemen.

328
00:22:15,120 --> 00:22:16,560
*bells tolling*

329
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,720
*cheerful carnival music*

330
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:22,840
(Policeman) Name?

331
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:24,000
Rath.

332
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,640
First name?

333
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:27,720
Gereon.

334
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:29,760
Date of birth?

335
00:22:30,360 --> 00:22:32,760
March 5th, 1899, in Cologne.

336
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:34,840
Can you identify yourself?

337
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:36,280
Unfortunately, no.

338
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:39,760
I would ask you
to telephone the Police President.

339
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:41,480
*he chuckles incredulously*

340
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:43,480
Engelbert Rath. My father.

341
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:46,240
*distant carnival music*

342
00:22:49,520 --> 00:22:52,520
You refuse to tell me what information
you possess?

343
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:53,720
I am not permitted to.

344
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:56,920
You are bound by doctor-patient confidentiality.

345
00:22:57,480 --> 00:22:59,320
I may only share it with colleagues.

346
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:02,880
Then I cannot procure papers for you.

347
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:06,680
Your acquaintance with my son
will not avail you either.

348
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:08,520
I had hoped

349
00:23:08,600 --> 00:23:11,040
you would use your contacts
with the Lord Mayor.

350
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:13,480
I cannot drag the Mayor into something

351
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,520
whose background I do not know.

352
00:23:16,920 --> 00:23:18,040
Then I must do it.

353
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:20,880
Do what you must.

354
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:25,360
Perhaps I should remind him
of that unsavory affair.

355
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:27,560
What affair?

356
00:23:27,720 --> 00:23:29,680
*mysterious piano music*

357
00:23:30,240 --> 00:23:33,160
The one for which you sent me to Berlin
in the first place.

358
00:23:33,240 --> 00:23:35,440
The Lord Mayor of Cologne is being blackmailed.

359
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,040
Dr. Adenauer.

360
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:38,840
*projector rattles*

361
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:41,960
The matter is unsavory.
Must be resolved before the election.

362
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:46,080
*phone rings*

363
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,760
*tense music*

364
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:52,000
*phone rings repeatedly*

365
00:23:57,640 --> 00:23:59,480
Yes, go ahead.
*music fades out*

366
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:01,560
Good day.
Detective Inspector Ritter,

367
00:24:01,640 --> 00:24:03,440
Department A,
Berlin Police Headquarters.

368
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:06,400
This concerns your son,
Inspector Gereon Rath.

369
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:09,360
He was last seen
on January 30th around 9 PM

370
00:24:09,440 --> 00:24:10,760
during a police operation

371
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:13,080
in the company of a murder suspect.

372
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:14,800
Since then, all trace is lost.

373
00:24:14,880 --> 00:24:16,960
What is your question, miss?

374
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:19,160
Have you heard from him?

375
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,200
No.

376
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:24,840
Not for years.

377
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:26,960
Thank you.

378
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:31,800
(Engelbert)
A Miss Ritter from Berlin.

379
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,080
She seems to miss you.

380
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:36,800
Our departure from Berlin was...

381
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:39,800
well, sudden.

382
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:43,480
You can't see the Mayor looking like that.

383
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:46,000
Not today on Rose Monday.
Frau Hülsenbeck!

384
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:48,080
Connect me with Berlin 1347.

385
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:51,800
(Kölsch) Hurry it up, you handsome devils,
or you'll miss the whole show.

386
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,200
Thank you.

387
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:55,760
There, this will suit you.

388
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:57,440
*he laughs*
Out of the question.

389
00:24:57,520 --> 00:25:00,160
If you want to reach France,
you need papers.

390
00:25:00,320 --> 00:25:02,120
Not dressed like this, however.

391
00:25:03,120 --> 00:25:04,600
*speaker talks indistinctly*

392
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:08,120
(Forster) I am not wearing that.

393
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:10,040
If you want to meet the Mayor,

394
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:12,080
you have to wear one of these.

395
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:14,040
(Woman)
No answer in Berlin.

396
00:25:14,120 --> 00:25:15,920
Thank you,
I'll try again later.

397
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:21,400
Lucky Frau Hülsenbeck could round this up
so quickly.

398
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:25,600
Come here,
give me a carnival peck.

399
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:29,000
Right, now let's have another drink, eh?

400
00:25:29,720 --> 00:25:31,640
Here's cheers!

401
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:32,800
*cheers*

402
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:34,440
(Announcer) Ladies and gentlemen,

403
00:25:34,600 --> 00:25:36,840
the city rises to the thunder of drums.

404
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:38,520
The squares are ablaze with light,

405
00:25:38,680 --> 00:25:41,440
and laughter hangs in the air like a promise.

406
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:43,480
From Alter Markt to Heumarkt,

407
00:25:43,560 --> 00:25:46,080
revelry rolls through the streets.

408
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:48,920
Music surges,
footsteps become rhythm,

409
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:51,520
motion turns into ecstasy.

410
00:25:51,600 --> 00:25:55,480
This is no mere moment,
this is an event.

411
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:56,640
Come on.

412
00:25:58,160 --> 00:26:00,160
Where?
We'll take a shortcut.

413
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:04,480
It's Carnival, it's Cologne,
and now the feast begins!

414
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:06,480
*carnival music, cheers*

415
00:26:07,680 --> 00:26:09,200
*amused laughter*

416
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:11,720
Up you go.

417
00:26:11,880 --> 00:26:13,880
*Forster groans with effort*

418
00:26:16,120 --> 00:26:17,760
*festive shouts*

419
00:26:25,840 --> 00:26:27,000
Kölle!

420
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:28,720
Kölle!

421
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:32,720
(Forster) We're losing sight of our goal,
Inspector.

422
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:38,600
There it is.
There is the brewery.

423
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:42,880
Over here, that's where the Mayor is sitting.

424
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:47,120
Don't be shy.

425
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:51,400
*patrons sing 'Einmal am Rhein'
by Willi Ostermann*

426
00:26:51,480 --> 00:26:59,760
# Once on the Rhine,
with a glass of wine in the pale moonshine #

427
00:26:59,840 --> 00:27:08,120
# Once on the Rhine,
you believe the whole world is thine #

428
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:16,520
# Your lips will laugh at any hour,
your ailing heart regains its power #

429
00:27:16,960 --> 00:27:24,240
# Come, let me invite you,
once on the Rhine #

430
00:27:24,320 --> 00:27:26,760
*song continues*
*singing in background*

431
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:29,040
(Adenauer in Kölsch dialect)
Saint Gereon in the flesh.

432
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:31,840
You bring me joy, my boy.
Herr Mayor.

433
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:34,040
Father.
Kölle Alaaf!

434
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:36,880
Here's the situation...
Papa has already filled me in.

435
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:41,760
You can fly with me to Paris tomorrow,
yes, at 8 o'clock sharp.

436
00:27:41,920 --> 00:27:44,800
I'm flying in an aeroplane,
must be back by evening.

437
00:27:46,120 --> 00:27:48,000
Thank you very much, Dr. Adenauer.

438
00:27:48,160 --> 00:27:50,680
When Papa says it's a must,
then it's a must, isn't it?

439
00:27:50,760 --> 00:27:53,000
It all works out in the end, boy.
Cheers!

440
00:27:53,080 --> 00:27:54,080
Cheers!

441
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:57,320
We're flying to Paris.

442
00:27:57,400 --> 00:27:58,440
What?
Yes.

443
00:27:58,520 --> 00:27:59,880
Tomorrow morning at eight.

444
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:03,480
Yes, we're in Cologne.
Everything works out here.

445
00:28:08,760 --> 00:28:12,120
*eerie sounds drown out carnival music*

446
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:28,360
Yes, operator?

447
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:31,640
SA Barracks Ehrenfeld, quickly.

448
00:28:31,800 --> 00:28:34,120
*carnival fanfare*

449
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:38,800
And now welcome with me
the new Reich Chancellor,

450
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:43,360
today in the dignified company
of Herr Otto Regensburger.

451
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:49,000
Thank you. Thank you.

452
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:53,160
Don't get your hopes up too soon,

453
00:28:53,320 --> 00:28:55,960
Herr Hitler and I...
- (Puppet) Regensburger!

454
00:28:56,120 --> 00:28:57,120
*audience laughs*

455
00:28:57,200 --> 00:29:00,400
Don't you dare associate yourself with me.

456
00:29:00,480 --> 00:29:03,600
Yes, but...
- We are the opposite of common.

457
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:06,760
You are entirely right,
Herr Reich Chancellor.

458
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:10,760
I've been trying to do that for a long time—
I mean, not to be common.

459
00:29:10,840 --> 00:29:11,920
*laughter*

460
00:29:12,080 --> 00:29:14,800
I mean, associate with you.
- Ah.

461
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:16,720
He always acts as if he doesn't know me.

462
00:29:16,800 --> 00:29:18,480
I don't know you at all.

463
00:29:19,080 --> 00:29:20,200
Let go of me!

464
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:21,560
Yes.

465
00:29:22,280 --> 00:29:25,040
That's going to be tricky,
Herr Reich Chancellor.

466
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:28,920
That is an order!

467
00:29:32,200 --> 00:29:33,720
(Regensburger) Wonderful!

468
00:29:33,800 --> 00:29:36,040
Ladies and gentlemen,
I told you before,

469
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:37,680
don't get your hopes up too soon.

470
00:29:37,760 --> 00:29:39,960
What do you mean,
don't get your hopes up?

471
00:29:40,040 --> 00:29:42,320
The people are delighted!
Thousands of laughs!

472
00:29:42,480 --> 00:29:44,160
Just for me!
- (Regensburger) No,

473
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:45,880
that last one was meant for me!
- What?

474
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:48,000
*astonished murmurs*

475
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:51,680
You're a Jew!

476
00:29:52,840 --> 00:29:55,000
Circumcised.

477
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:57,400
*laughter, carnival fanfare*

478
00:29:57,560 --> 00:30:00,040
You're entirely right,
Herr Reich Chancellor.

479
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:01,280
I, on the other hand...

480
00:30:01,360 --> 00:30:03,760
Yes, you on the other hand?
- Yes, I on the other hand...

481
00:30:03,840 --> 00:30:05,000
*roars of laughter*

482
00:30:07,640 --> 00:30:09,080
(Regensburger) Thank you very much.

483
00:30:11,320 --> 00:30:14,720
Today the Herr Reich Chancellor
will grace us with a reading,

484
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:16,760
from his book.

485
00:30:16,920 --> 00:30:19,800
*boos*
Yes, a polemic...

486
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:22,160
(Puppet) Mein Kampf!
- (Woman) Get the hell out of here!

487
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:24,080
*indignant shouts*

488
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:27,080
Please, please, quiet!
Quiet please, ladies and gentlemen!

489
00:30:27,240 --> 00:30:31,000
Here is a guest so enthusiastic that he...

490
00:30:32,440 --> 00:30:34,040
*festive music*

491
00:30:34,520 --> 00:30:35,720
Out with it, yes!

492
00:30:41,400 --> 00:30:42,400
Alaaf!

493
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:05,600
*music plays softly in background*

494
00:31:07,680 --> 00:31:08,680
Well...

495
00:31:08,840 --> 00:31:11,800
*guests hum along to melody*

496
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:26,200
*glasses clinking*

497
00:31:37,720 --> 00:31:40,800
Dr. Forster, we have to go.
The SA is back there. Out of here.

498
00:31:57,800 --> 00:31:59,640
*music slows down*

499
00:32:00,680 --> 00:32:02,920
*powerful drumbeats*

500
00:32:14,800 --> 00:32:17,120
*music continues*

501
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:25,760
*quiet, inaudible dialogue*

502
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:27,880
...summoned to Paris.

503
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:30,640
In eight hours, the Schnüsse Tring meets.

504
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:33,760
Well, what do the French understand
of the good life anyway.

505
00:32:34,560 --> 00:32:37,600
See to it that you're back home in time
for the election,

506
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:40,080
to stop that narcissistic rabble.

507
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:42,200
Am I right, Gereon?

508
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:45,200
(muffled) Gereon, am I right?

509
00:32:46,040 --> 00:32:49,240
(muffled) Luckily you just survived
the massacre, my boy.

510
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:51,880
*engine roar drowns out Adenauer*

511
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:13,600
Monsieur Fiquet,
it is a pleasure to see you.

512
00:33:14,440 --> 00:33:18,000
Weather isn't great today,
but that's no different in Cologne, is it?

513
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:21,480
We have little time, unfortunately.
*interpreter speaks French*

514
00:33:21,560 --> 00:33:24,000
Urgent official business awaits me in Cologne.

515
00:33:24,080 --> 00:33:25,760
I must be back by evening.

516
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:27,440
*interpreter speaks*

517
00:33:27,520 --> 00:33:30,200
*Fiquet speaks French*

518
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:39,240
With the French, one must always reckon
with the weakness of the flesh.

519
00:33:39,400 --> 00:33:41,560
Allow me to introduce myself.

520
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:43,560
Eduard von Kittlitz,
German Embassy, Paris.

521
00:33:43,720 --> 00:33:46,240
Your companions,
Herr Lord Mayor,

522
00:33:46,320 --> 00:33:47,640
I fear...

523
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:51,160
I have directives from Berlin,
Your Excellency. Here.

524
00:33:51,320 --> 00:33:52,720
*interpreter speaks*

525
00:33:53,280 --> 00:33:55,240
From the Reich Ministry of the Interior.

526
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:59,520
Reich Minister Göring, with respect.
I must ask you to follow me.

527
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:01,840
Hold on, Herr Kittlitz,
one moment please.

528
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:05,120
I need to examine
what you have handed me first.

529
00:34:06,840 --> 00:34:08,120
*ominous music*

530
00:34:09,159 --> 00:34:13,040
Very well. These gentlemen come with me,
they are part of my delegation.

531
00:34:13,199 --> 00:34:14,800
No, no.
- Monsieur Fiquet.

532
00:34:14,880 --> 00:34:17,719
Would you be so kind
as to inspect their papers now?

533
00:34:17,800 --> 00:34:20,360
I would be very grateful.
Kittlitz, good day to you.

534
00:34:22,280 --> 00:34:24,560
Inspector, Professor, come with me.

535
00:34:24,639 --> 00:34:27,840
You take the red motorcar.
*man speaks French*

536
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:36,120
*car starts*

537
00:34:38,400 --> 00:34:39,960
*man speaks French*

538
00:34:40,120 --> 00:34:42,040
I do not understand your language.

539
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:46,080
*music fades out*

540
00:34:47,600 --> 00:34:50,920
*bells tolling,
distant chatter*

541
00:35:02,200 --> 00:35:03,960
*somber music*

542
00:35:06,360 --> 00:35:07,360
Merci.

543
00:35:09,920 --> 00:35:12,640
*French conversations in background*

544
00:35:13,400 --> 00:35:15,320
*street sounds*

545
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:17,160
*French conversation*

546
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:31,120
(MC in German)
Paris is Berlin.

547
00:35:33,320 --> 00:35:34,320
Pardon.

548
00:35:35,080 --> 00:35:36,200
*singing in French*

549
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:45,400
Dr. Weiß?

550
00:35:46,320 --> 00:35:49,520
Are you Dr. Weiß?
- With whom do I have the honor?

551
00:35:50,160 --> 00:35:52,240
Edmund Forster. A pleasure.

552
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:55,120
Who is this?
- Inspector Rath.

553
00:35:55,280 --> 00:35:58,640
He guided me here, thankfully.

554
00:35:59,560 --> 00:36:01,600
I will not speak with a police officer,

555
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:03,280
let alone one from Germany.

556
00:36:03,440 --> 00:36:04,440
No.

557
00:36:05,520 --> 00:36:06,520
Dr. Weiß,

558
00:36:07,800 --> 00:36:10,840
Inspector Rath risked a great deal

559
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:13,000
to bring me here to you.

560
00:36:13,080 --> 00:36:15,320
We can trust him.

561
00:36:16,560 --> 00:36:17,760
Rath, did you say?

562
00:36:18,400 --> 00:36:21,320
I believe you knew my brother,
Anno Rath.

563
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:24,440
He studied under Dr. Forster in Berlin.

564
00:36:24,840 --> 00:36:26,160
Anno Rath is your brother?

565
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:28,560
Yes, he sent us to you.

566
00:36:29,440 --> 00:36:30,920
Anno Rath is dead.

567
00:36:32,120 --> 00:36:33,480
It's complicated.

568
00:36:36,200 --> 00:36:37,200
(Forster) Yes.

569
00:36:38,280 --> 00:36:41,280
Thank you.
- Would you like something to drink?

570
00:36:41,440 --> 00:36:42,960
Most gladly.
Yes, please.

571
00:36:43,120 --> 00:36:44,200
Mademoiselle.

572
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:51,040
When did you last see my brother?

573
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:56,240
In August '24, during that fateful lecture,

574
00:36:56,400 --> 00:36:58,880
when your brother presented
his doctoral dissertation.

575
00:36:58,960 --> 00:37:02,800
...which illustrates the impact our research

576
00:37:03,560 --> 00:37:05,320
can have on politics as well.

577
00:37:05,400 --> 00:37:06,840
*sinister music*

578
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:09,720
Currently, the Munich Public Prosecutor's Office
must decide

579
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:12,880
whether the man imprisoned after his coup
last year,

580
00:37:13,040 --> 00:37:14,160
Adolf Hitler,

581
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:18,400
may be released early
from fortress confinement.

582
00:37:18,960 --> 00:37:22,480
For this reason, Senior Prosecutor
Dr. Martin Dresse

583
00:37:22,640 --> 00:37:25,440
approached our faculty

584
00:37:26,160 --> 00:37:28,280
and requested an expert psychological assessment.

585
00:37:29,880 --> 00:37:31,200
Lance Corporal Hitler,

586
00:37:31,720 --> 00:37:34,000
photographed here shortly after his admission

587
00:37:34,080 --> 00:37:37,960
to the Pasewalk Reserve Hospital
in October 1918.

588
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:40,000
Blinded, by his own account,

589
00:37:40,080 --> 00:37:44,040
by a British mustard gas shell.

590
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:49,160
His treating psychiatrist,
Dr. Edmund Forster,

591
00:37:49,320 --> 00:37:53,640
identified Hitler in the clinic
as a hysteric,

592
00:37:53,800 --> 00:37:55,920
who, through auto-suggestion,

593
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:58,640
fantasized himself into imaginary blindness.

594
00:37:58,800 --> 00:38:00,000
*door opens*

595
00:38:00,080 --> 00:38:01,800
In his clinical report...

596
00:38:03,040 --> 00:38:05,200
*screams of agony*

597
00:38:11,480 --> 00:38:13,720
*acid hisses*

598
00:38:13,880 --> 00:38:15,600
*dramatic music*

599
00:38:16,560 --> 00:38:17,880
Hence your scars.

600
00:38:19,640 --> 00:38:20,640
Yes.

601
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:26,640
I always saw this as a reminder

602
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:30,680
of my former hospital comrade.

603
00:38:31,640 --> 00:38:34,400
The scars remind me of him.

604
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:37,960
For many years, every single day.

605
00:38:38,760 --> 00:38:41,360
After that attack, you changed your name.

606
00:38:41,920 --> 00:38:42,920
Yes.

607
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:46,440
He must believe that I died.

608
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:49,680
(Weiß) Who would have thought
that the medical history

609
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:52,200
of an insignificant Austrian corporal

610
00:38:52,840 --> 00:38:55,720
would prove to be of such decisive significance?

611
00:38:57,320 --> 00:38:59,800
My brother said you possess
trusted connections

612
00:38:59,880 --> 00:39:02,320
to influential French daily newspapers.

613
00:39:02,480 --> 00:39:03,480
Indeed.

614
00:39:04,520 --> 00:39:06,880
The press has been waiting for a story like this.

615
00:39:07,040 --> 00:39:09,760
Yes. The world must learn as quickly
as possible

616
00:39:09,840 --> 00:39:11,960
whom they are dealing with in Germany.

617
00:39:12,520 --> 00:39:13,520
That is true.

618
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:17,400
Yet whether that will deter our countrymen

619
00:39:17,560 --> 00:39:19,920
from voting for the man,
I venture to doubt.

620
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:21,760
The brutality with which they attempt

621
00:39:21,840 --> 00:39:23,720
to keep this information secret

622
00:39:23,800 --> 00:39:26,280
speaks of profound alarm
within the NSDAP.

623
00:39:29,760 --> 00:39:32,880
Good. Then we should get straight to work.

624
00:39:39,960 --> 00:39:41,760
From now on, he is under my protection.

625
00:39:41,920 --> 00:39:42,960
Understood.

626
00:39:43,040 --> 00:39:45,040
Come, there is a back exit.

627
00:39:46,800 --> 00:39:49,640
Gereon, thank you, and...

628
00:39:50,520 --> 00:39:52,200
take care of yourself.

629
00:39:52,840 --> 00:39:53,920
Good luck.

630
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:56,240
*glasses clinking*

631
00:39:58,320 --> 00:39:59,840
Farewell.
This way.

632
00:40:01,240 --> 00:40:03,760
*quiet background chatter*

633
00:40:05,760 --> 00:40:07,400
*sinister music*

634
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:11,840
Why did Gereon never tell me about you?

635
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:16,000
Because knowledge of my existence is dangerous.

636
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:18,960
*sigh*

637
00:40:19,560 --> 00:40:20,680
For everyone.

638
00:40:20,760 --> 00:40:21,960
*applause*

639
00:40:24,320 --> 00:40:26,600
(Guests) Bravo.

640
00:40:35,720 --> 00:40:37,080
*laughter*

641
00:40:37,240 --> 00:40:39,120
*echoing splashing*

642
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:43,680
*jazz music with spoken singing*

643
00:40:43,840 --> 00:40:46,560
*"Zu Asche, Zu Staub"
by Severija Janušauskaitė*

644
00:40:47,560 --> 00:40:48,920
*applause*

645
00:40:56,600 --> 00:40:58,880
# To ashes, to dust #

646
00:41:00,560 --> 00:41:02,680
# Stolen from the light #

647
00:41:04,160 --> 00:41:11,120
# Yet not just yet,
miracles wait until the end #

648
00:41:12,480 --> 00:41:13,920
*ethereal sounds*

649
00:41:17,320 --> 00:41:18,720
*audience claps along*

650
00:41:18,800 --> 00:41:21,560
# Ocean of time #

651
00:41:22,440 --> 00:41:24,600
# Eternal law #

652
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:28,440
# To ashes, to dust #

653
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:34,360
# To ashes,
yet not just yet #

654
00:41:39,480 --> 00:41:41,360
*singer vocalizes*

655
00:41:46,280 --> 00:41:48,040
# To ashes, to dust #

656
00:41:50,040 --> 00:41:52,160
# Stolen from the light #

657
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:56,320
# Yet not just yet #

658
00:41:58,120 --> 00:42:01,240
# Miracles wait until the end #

659
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:03,200
*singer vocalizes soulfully*

660
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:15,480
# It is but a dream #

661
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:20,440
Mere chasing after the wind

662
00:42:21,120 --> 00:42:25,160
# Who knows for certain? #

663
00:42:27,440 --> 00:42:30,720
# The clock upon your wall #

664
00:42:31,200 --> 00:42:34,680
# Is filled with sand #

665
00:42:34,760 --> 00:42:37,600
# Place your hand in mine #

666
00:42:38,480 --> 00:42:41,800
# And let us be eternal #

667
00:42:42,480 --> 00:42:45,800
# Now you make your choice #

668
00:42:45,880 --> 00:42:50,440
# Casting us
between bliss and torment #

669
00:42:50,520 --> 00:42:54,560
# Yet can I forgive you #

670
00:42:56,800 --> 00:42:59,440
# You are so near to death #

671
00:43:00,640 --> 00:43:04,160
# And yet your gaze so clear #

672
00:43:04,240 --> 00:43:08,000
# Recognize me, I am ready #

673
00:43:08,160 --> 00:43:13,800
# Seeking immortality #

674
00:43:17,880 --> 00:43:19,600
*ominous music*

675
00:43:21,600 --> 00:43:23,080
(Woman) Bravo!

676
00:43:33,040 --> 00:43:35,120
*women laugh uproariously*

677
00:43:36,040 --> 00:43:37,200
*gun clicks*

678
00:43:39,680 --> 00:43:41,360
Good evening, Inspector Rath.

679
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:44,000
*

